# Point labels on graphs

When a plotted graph is **increasing** near a marked point, place the label with `anchor=west` at the **exact point coordinates**. Do not offset the node away from the point.

```latex
% ✅ increasing graph: west of the exact point (Figure 6.7.1)
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:0,0) {absolute min};

% ❌ do not invent an offset for an increasing graph
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:0.15,0.28) {absolute min};
```

Use `fill=white` only when the text would otherwise sit on a line. Major overlaps only; do not fine-tune endlessly.
